These are the solutions to the problem from other agents: To find the highest point of the trajectory for a given angle $\theta$, we need to determine the time $t$ when the projectile reaches its maximum height. This occurs when the vertical component of the velocity becomes zero.

The vertical component of the velocity at any time $t$ is given by:
\[ v_y(t) = v \sin \theta - gt. \]

Setting $v_y(t) = 0$ gives us the time at which the projectile reaches its maximum height:
